1
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,039
Mom!

2
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:56,360
Mom!

3
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,479
I got in!

4
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:00,800
South University of Political Science and Law!

5
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,199
Shitou,

6
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,599
you've really made something of yourself!

7
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,599
Open it up and show Mom.

8
00:04:13,719 --> 00:04:15,599
Look, the Department of Law!

9
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:31,879
Mom's not crying. I sold these

10
00:04:32,279 --> 00:04:33,560
salted duck eggs for you.

11
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,399
Take this.

12
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:35,519
No need, Mom.

13
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,959
I still have plenty of clothes.

14
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:37,480
It's enough.

15
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:40,639
No, you need new clothes for college.

16
00:04:40,959 --> 00:04:42,439
How can you wear old ones?

17
00:04:48,519 --> 00:04:49,399
Get on the bus.

18
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:50,639
Mom,

19
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:52,879
take good care of yourself at home.

20
00:04:53,879 --> 00:04:54,839
Don't worry.

21
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,959
I always take good care of myself.

22
00:05:06,319 --> 00:05:06,959
Go on.

23
00:05:27,639 --> 00:05:28,439
Shitou.

24
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:32,319
Take care of yourself.

25
00:06:38,839 --> 00:06:39,959
Officer Meng, you're here.

26
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:42,040
Hello.

27
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,519
Let me look at you.

28
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,040
I must say,

29
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,720
after all these years,

30
00:06:50,279 --> 00:06:52,360
you really haven't changed.

31
00:06:53,199 --> 00:06:55,000
No way. Please sit.

32
00:06:58,639 --> 00:06:59,480
Have some tea.

33
00:06:59,639 --> 00:07:00,040
All right.

34
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:00,920
Thanks.

35
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,160
What good tea do you have?

36
00:07:03,199 --> 00:07:04,160
This tea...

37
00:07:04,639 --> 00:07:05,720
my son-in-law

38
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,600
brought it back from a trip to Yunnan.

39
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:08,920
It's really good.

40
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:14,160
I'll have some.

41
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:15,680
It's quite good.

42
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,399
How are the kids doing?

43
00:07:21,279 --> 00:07:21,879
Good.

44
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:25,480
My son just started college,

45
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:29,519
and my daughter's having a baby soon.

46
00:07:29,839 --> 00:07:30,600
Really?

47
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,920
Then you'll be a grandmother soon.

48
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,600
Here,

49
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:38,759
congratulations!

50
00:07:50,519 --> 00:07:52,639
Old Li's second son,

51
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,199
you know him?

52
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,040
Yeah.

53
00:07:59,079 --> 00:08:00,800
He's not as decent as the village chief.

54
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,120
I heard

55
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,439
the family money went straight to his head.

56
00:08:06,199 --> 00:08:07,199
He causes trouble everywhere.

57
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,480
The village chief worries about him too.

58
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,279
Yeah.

59
00:08:13,399 --> 00:08:15,120
Money is definitely a good thing,

60
00:08:16,279 --> 00:08:17,319
but sometimes,

61
00:08:19,639 --> 00:08:20,920
it only ruins things.

62
00:08:24,319 --> 00:08:25,079
What happened?

63
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,120
He lost money gambling.

64
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:29,839
Lost his temper

65
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:32,039
and stabbed someone.

66
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:35,080
Is it serious?

67
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:38,360
Depends on his luck.

68
00:08:40,399 --> 00:08:41,519
The victim who got stabbed

69
00:08:41,519 --> 00:08:42,679
is still fighting for his life.

70
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,519
Whether it ends in severe injury

71
00:08:45,519 --> 00:08:46,759
or death,

72
00:08:47,679 --> 00:08:48,759
it all comes down to fate.

73
00:08:52,679 --> 00:08:53,879
The kid is terrified of dying.

74
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:56,720
He's desperate to earn credit,

75
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,080
wanting to report and expose someone.

76
00:09:02,639 --> 00:09:03,639
Expose what?

77
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,480
Your whole village knew

78
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,080
that you killed your husband

79
00:09:25,279 --> 00:09:26,080
and buried him.

80
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,879
When Old Li heard his son say that,

81
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:35,679
he went up and slapped him.

82
00:09:39,639 --> 00:09:40,440
Good.

83
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,600
Earlier discipline could've avoided this.

84
00:09:44,279 --> 00:09:46,480
People in your village love to gossip,

85
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,200
but when it came to your case,

86
00:09:51,519 --> 00:09:53,559
no one brought it up all these years.

87
00:09:55,879 --> 00:09:57,600
Everyone maintained a collective silence.

88
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,679
Quite a united front.

89
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:04,360
Indeed.

90
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,159
Will reporting it reduce his sentence?

91
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,840
That's up to the judge.

92
00:10:17,039 --> 00:10:17,799
However,

93
00:10:19,639 --> 00:10:21,039
reporting a murder

94
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,720
counts as redeeming oneself through meritorious service.

95
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,399
It should help.

96
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:32,720
That's good.

97
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,039
As the person involved,

98
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:39,039
if you make a Voluntary surrender,

99
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:43,480
you can also seek leniency.

100
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,240
Can you tell me...

101
00:10:55,399 --> 00:10:56,200
where you...

102
00:10:57,799 --> 00:10:58,600
buried him?

103
00:11:02,279 --> 00:11:03,000
I didn't bury him.

104
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,000
Then where is he?

105
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,679
I salted him.

106
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,679
Just like salting duck eggs.

107
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,840
Where... Where is he?

108
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,720
Right inside that vat.

109
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:46,840
You did this alone?

110
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,240
Yeah.

111
00:11:51,159 --> 00:11:52,200
It's better that way.

112
00:11:54,799 --> 00:11:56,720
Keeps others out of it.

113
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:16,919
This really is good tea.

114
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:19,720
I'll have another cup.

115
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:20,440
Here you go.

116
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,000
Officer Meng,

117
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:36,600
when do I leave?

118
00:15:03,879 --> 00:15:04,679
Officer Meng,

119
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,840
have you ever felt that

120
00:15:08,639 --> 00:15:09,639
the evil in human nature

121
00:15:10,879 --> 00:15:13,159
isn't as obvious as a lunging beast?

122
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,559
It's always wrapped in hardship,

123
00:15:18,759 --> 00:15:19,559
grievance,

124
00:15:20,279 --> 00:15:20,840
agony,

125
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,919
even family ties and love.

126
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:27,399
It says,

127
00:15:28,279 --> 00:15:29,759
"I had no choice."

128
00:15:32,399 --> 00:15:33,679
It makes you think,

129
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,799
"This isn't my fault."

130
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,080
But in the end,

131
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,120
the knife

132
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,679
was raised by their own hands.

133
00:15:45,399 --> 00:15:46,320
The blood

134
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,000
belonged to their family.

135
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:50,919
The crime

136
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,240
was committed with full awareness.

137
00:15:58,399 --> 00:15:59,799
They aren't lunatics,

138
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:02,000
nor are they demons.

139
00:16:02,919 --> 00:16:03,879
They're human beings.

140
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,200
Just like me,

141
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:09,080
they're human.

142
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,519
If human nature is inherently evil,

143
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:17,039
merely suppressed by discipline

144
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:18,279
and kept in check,

145
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,960
then are you really redeeming them,

146
00:16:24,039 --> 00:16:25,600
or just deceiving yourselves?

147
00:16:31,639 --> 00:16:32,440
Dongmei,

148
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,000
that doesn't sound like you at all.

149
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,679
It wasn't me who said it.

150
00:16:44,759 --> 00:16:45,759
I just saw it the other day,

151
00:16:45,759 --> 00:16:47,279
written in Shitou's notebook.

152
00:16:50,519 --> 00:16:51,559
I don't understand the law.

153
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,159
You're a police officer,

154
00:16:55,519 --> 00:16:56,799
so I wanted to ask you for him.

155
00:17:01,679 --> 00:17:03,960
I'm just a grassroots cop.

156
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:07,799
As for my duty?

157
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,559
It's just to do my best

158
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:15,079
and do my job well.

159
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:50,480
Whatever they charge is their business,

160
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,839
but if you stay here, you just pay up.

161
00:17:53,759 --> 00:17:54,279
Officer Meng!

162
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,039
Look at all this...

163
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,920
I rushed over after getting the letter.

164
00:17:57,119 --> 00:17:58,880
What's going on here now?

165
00:17:59,240 --> 00:17:59,559
Here's the situation.

166
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,160
Young Shitou here...

167
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,000
Shitou,

168
00:18:02,319 --> 00:18:03,359
he's grown so tall now.

169
00:18:03,759 --> 00:18:05,400
When he heard Dongmei was arrested,

170
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,039
he took a leave from school and came back,

171
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,519
asking everyone to write a Joint clemency petition,

172
00:18:10,119 --> 00:18:11,799
saying a Joint clemency petition could save Dongmei.

173
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:12,359
Anyway,

174
00:18:12,799 --> 00:18:15,359
that's why the representatives are all here,

175
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,359
preparing to write a Joint clemency petition

176
00:18:17,359 --> 00:18:18,519
signed by the whole village.

177
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,440
Let me go talk to the boy.

178
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:21,799
Okay.

179
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:22,279
All right.

180
00:18:22,279 --> 00:18:23,160
Have a good talk with him.

181
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,519
How's law school?

182
00:18:28,279 --> 00:18:29,119
What year are you in?

183
00:18:29,839 --> 00:18:30,440
Senior year.

184
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,319
Senior year, huh.

185
00:18:31,759 --> 00:18:32,799
Almost graduating, then?
